n Earl Ralf 428; on William Malet 430; on the Conqueror&#8217;s earldoms 429; his Domesday errors and confusion 151, 425, 428, 436-7, 445-8, 463; on the &#8216;Civic League&#8217; 433-5; his wild dream 438; his special interest in Exeter 431; on legends 441; on Thierry 451, 458; his method 454-5; on Lisois 460; on Stigand 461; on Walter Tirel 476-7; on St. Hugh&#8217;s action [1197] 528; on the Winchester Assembly 535-8; distorts feudalism 537; on the king&#8217;s court 538; on Richard&#8217;s change of seal 540; necessity of criticising his work, xi., 353.
